/-!
# THE DRIFT, PRICED PER CUBE — against the LOCAL PURE-GAUGE reference.

Lane `compute/drift_percube/`.  Write scope: that directory only.  Never `lake build`.

`compute/recompose_sum/` removed the GLOBAL covariance threshold by summing per-cube gauged
smallness over a disjoint cover (`LocFeed.global_floor_from_percube_gauges`).  The drift price
`κ = 4√2·α₁(U)` that `compute/hrawr_discharge/` had to feed the chain is still GLOBAL and still
UNGAUGED: `HrawRDischarge.terminal_sum_at_star_datum` carries `hdrift : α₁(V) ≤ 1/(13336·ℓ³)`.

This module asks the floor's question of the drift and answers the half of it that is TRUE.

## THE ANSWER, IN ONE LINE

The drift localizes and sums exactly as the floor does — **but only against a reference background
that is transported with the gauge.**  With one unrelated gauge `γ i` per cube, the quantity that
per-cube gauged smallness controls is

>  `∑_i ∑_{p ∈ □_i} ‖(D_U − D_{W_i})A(p)‖² ≤ 128·α²·∑_b ‖A b‖²`,   `W_i := 1^{γ_i⁻¹}`

the drift of `U` against the **local pure gauge** `W_i`, NOT against the flat background `1`.
`128 = 32·4`: `32` is `RegularUPerturbation.plaqEnergy_curlDrift_le`'s constant, cited through
`LocDrift.local_curlDrift_le`, and `4` is the enlarged-cube bond multiplicity
`bondsOn_tilde_mult_le_four`, proved here by the method of `LocSum.tilde_mult_le_four` (REUSED).
In operator terms the per-cube price is `8√2·α`, exactly twice the global `4√2·α₁` — the factor is
`√4`, the multiplicity, and nothing else.

`stage/DriftNoGo.lean` proves that the gap between `W_i` and `1` is NOT closable: it is a pure
gauge, per-cube gauged data cannot see it at any radius, and it moves the flat-referenced drift by
an amount bounded below.

## WHAT IS NEW HERE AND WHAT IS CITED

New: `relDrift` (the drift against a general reference), the gauge identity `relDrift_eq_gauged`,
the per-cube bound `local_relDrift_le`, the bond multiplicity `bondsOn_tilde_mult_le_four`, the
summation `global_drift_from_percube_gauges`, and the partition control `plaqsOn_family_card_eq_one`.
Cited and not re-derived: `32` (`plaqEnergy_curlDrift_le` via `LocDrift`), the stencil
(`LocDrift.pathSite_mem_block_or_next`), `4` (`LocSum.tilde_mult_le_four`), gauge covariance of the
covariant curl (`AlphaAnalyticity.curlValueCovariant_gauge`), and `‖R(g)X‖ = ‖X‖`
(`AlphaAnalyticity.norm_RMap`).

**Nothing here is graded by this lane (BUILD DISCIPLINE 8): it reports facts.  The gates adjudicate.**

## ISLAND / MERGE STATUS (measured)

Nothing in this lane is installed in `formal/`; nothing enters `Spine.lean`'s import cone; nothing
contributes to `FULL3D.main`'s axiom set.  The staged modules are islands importing other islands.
Merging is a separate, unattempted step.
-/

namespace AdalyFormal.Balaban.DriftPerCube

open Finset
open AdalyFormal.Target.ClayStatement
open AdalyFormal.Balaban.AdmissibleSubspace
open AdalyFormal.Balaban.CovariantOperators
open AdalyFormal.Balaban.CovariantHjMinimizer (trivialU)
open AdalyFormal.Balaban.RegularUPerturbation
open AdalyFormal.Balaban.AlphaAnalyticity (GaugeFn gaugeActA gaugeActA_apply gaugeInv gaugeMul
  gaugeTransform_comp gaugeTransform_one curlValueCovariant_gauge norm_RMap)
open AdalyFormal.Balaban.LocalizedEstimates

variable {L : PeriodicLatticeExtent} {ell : ℕ}

/-! ## §1 — THE PURE GAUGE, AND THE DRIFT AGAINST A GENERAL REFERENCE -/

/-- **The pure gauge generated by `γ`**: `1^γ(b) = γ(b₋)·γ(b₊)⁻¹`.  This is the background the
per-cube gauged class actually localizes `U` against — see `§3`. -/
noncomputable def pureGauge (γ : GaugeFn L) :
    PeriodicLinkConfiguration (Matrix.specialUnitaryGroup (Fin 2) ℂ) L :=
  periodicGaugeTransform γ (trivialU L)

theorem pureGauge_apply (γ : GaugeFn L) (b : Bond L) :
    pureGauge γ b = γ b.1 * (γ (periodicLatticeShift b.1 b.2))⁻¹ := by
  show γ b.1 * (1 : Matrix.specialUnitaryGroup (Fin 2) ℂ)
      * (γ (periodicLatticeShift b.1 b.2))⁻¹ = _
  rw [mul_one]

/-- The pure gauge of the trivial gauge is the flat background: the reference below CONTAINS the
chain's flat one as the case `γ = 1`. -/
theorem pureGauge_one : pureGauge (fun _ => (1 : Matrix.specialUnitaryGroup (Fin 2) ℂ))
    = trivialU L := gaugeTransform_one (trivialU L)

/-- **THE DRIFT AGAINST A REFERENCE BACKGROUND `W`**: `(D_U − D_W)A`.  At `W = 1` this is
`RegularUPerturbation.curlDrift`, definitionally (`curlDrift_eq_relDrift`). -/
noncomputable def relDrift (U W : PeriodicLinkConfiguration (Matrix.specialUnitaryGroup (Fin 2) ℂ) L)
    (A : Bond L → SuTwo) : PeriodicLatticePlaquette L → SuTwo :=
  curlValueCovariant U A - curlValueCovariant W A

theorem relDrift_apply
    (U W : PeriodicLinkConfiguration (Matrix.specialUnitaryGroup (Fin 2) ℂ) L)
    (A : Bond L → SuTwo) (p : PeriodicLatticePlaquette L) :
    relDrift U W A p = curlValueCovariant U A p - curlValueCovariant W A p := rfl

/-- **The chain's drift is the `W = 1` case**, so nothing below changes the object under study. -/
theorem curlDrift_eq_relDrift
    (U : PeriodicLinkConfiguration (Matrix.specialUnitaryGroup (Fin 2) ℂ) L)
    (A : Bond L → SuTwo) : curlDrift U A = relDrift U (trivialU L) A := rfl

/-! ## §2 — THE GAUGE IDENTITY: the gauged flat drift IS the relative drift at the original `U` -/

theorem gaugeMul_inv_right (γ : GaugeFn L) :
    gaugeMul γ (gaugeInv γ) = fun _ => (1 : Matrix.specialUnitaryGroup (Fin 2) ℂ) := by
  funext x; simp [gaugeMul, gaugeInv]

/-- **Gauging the local pure-gauge reference flattens it**: `(1^{γ⁻¹})^γ = 1`. -/
theorem gauge_pureGauge_inv (γ : GaugeFn L) :
    periodicGaugeTransform γ (pureGauge (gaugeInv γ)) = trivialU L := by
  unfold pureGauge
  rw [gaugeTransform_comp, gaugeMul_inv_right, gaugeTransform_one]

/-- **THE IDENTITY THIS MODULE TURNS ON.**  The FLAT-referenced drift of the GAUGED data is the
`R(γ)`-rotation of the PURE-GAUGE-referenced drift of the ORIGINAL data:

>  `(D_{U^γ} − D_1)(A^γ)(p) = R(γ(p₀)) · (D_U − D_{1^{γ⁻¹}})(A)(p)`.

Every step is a citation: `curlValueCovariant_gauge` twice, and `gauge_pureGauge_inv` to present
`1` as the gauge transform of the pure-gauge reference. -/
theorem relDrift_eq_gauged (γ : GaugeFn L)
    (U : PeriodicLinkConfiguration (Matrix.specialUnitaryGroup (Fin 2) ℂ) L)
    (A : Bond L → SuTwo) (p : PeriodicLatticePlaquette L) :
    curlDrift (periodicGaugeTransform γ U) (gaugeActA γ A) p
      = RMap (γ p.1) (relDrift U (pureGauge (gaugeInv γ)) A p) := by
  have hflat : curlValueCovariant (trivialU L) (gaugeActA γ A) p
      = RMap (γ p.1) (curlValueCovariant (pureGauge (gaugeInv γ)) A p) := by
    conv_lhs => rw [← gauge_pureGauge_inv γ]
    rw [curlValueCovariant_gauge]
  show curlValueCovariant (periodicGaugeTransform γ U) (gaugeActA γ A) p
      - curlValueCovariant (trivialU L) (gaugeActA γ A) p = _
  rw [curlValueCovariant_gauge, hflat, relDrift_apply, map_sub]

/-- The same identity in norms — `R(γ)` is an isometry, so the two drifts are EQUAL in size,
plaquette by plaquette.  No inequality is spent here. -/
theorem norm_relDrift_eq (γ : GaugeFn L)
    (U : PeriodicLinkConfiguration (Matrix.specialUnitaryGroup (Fin 2) ℂ) L)
    (A : Bond L → SuTwo) (p : PeriodicLatticePlaquette L) :
    ‖relDrift U (pureGauge (gaugeInv γ)) A p‖
      = ‖curlDrift (periodicGaugeTransform γ U) (gaugeActA γ A) p‖ := by
  rw [relDrift_eq_gauged, norm_RMap]

/-! ## §3 — THE PER-CUBE BOUND: local index set AND local, GAUGED smallness -/

/-- **THE DRIFT, LOCALIZED AND GAUGED.**  For one cube `Y`, one gauge `γ`, and `α` bounding the
holonomy deviations of the LOCALLY GAUGED background `U^γ` on the cube's own bonds:

>  `∑_{p ∈ plaqsOn Y} ‖(D_U − D_{1^{γ⁻¹}})A(p)‖² ≤ 32·α²·∑_{b ∈ bondsOn (□̃ Y)} ‖A b‖²`.

The conclusion is at the ORIGINAL `U` and the ORIGINAL `A`; the gauge appears only in the
REFERENCE and in the hypothesis.  `32` is cited (`LocDrift.local_curlDrift_le`). -/
theorem local_relDrift_le (hell2 : 2 ≤ ell) (hdvd : ∀ μ : Fin 3, ell ∣ (L μ + 1))
    (U : PeriodicLinkConfiguration (Matrix.specialUnitaryGroup (Fin 2) ℂ) L)
    (A : Bond L → SuTwo) (γ : GaugeFn L) (α : ℝ) (hα0 : 0 ≤ α) (Y : Finset (CSite L ell))
    (hα : ∀ b ∈ bondsOn Y, RMapLipschitz.frobNorm
      (((periodicGaugeTransform γ U) b : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) - 1) ≤ α) :
    ∑ p ∈ plaqsOn Y, ‖relDrift U (pureGauge (gaugeInv γ)) A p‖ ^ 2
      ≤ 32 * α ^ 2 * ∑ b ∈ bondsOn (tilde hdvd Y), ‖A b‖ ^ 2 := by
  have h := local_curlDrift_le hell2 hdvd (periodicGaugeTransform γ U) (gaugeActA γ A) α hα0 Y hα
  have hL : ∑ p ∈ plaqsOn Y, ‖relDrift U (pureGauge (gaugeInv γ)) A p‖ ^ 2
      = ∑ p ∈ plaqsOn Y, ‖curlDrift (periodicGaugeTransform γ U) (gaugeActA γ A) p‖ ^ 2 :=
    Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun p _ => by rw [norm_relDrift_eq])
  have hR : ∑ b ∈ bondsOn (tilde hdvd Y), ‖gaugeActA γ A b‖ ^ 2
      = ∑ b ∈ bondsOn (tilde hdvd Y), ‖A b‖ ^ 2 :=
    Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun b _ => by rw [gaugeActA_apply, norm_RMap])
  rw [hL]
  rwa [hR] at h

/-! ## §4 — THE BOND MULTIPLICITY OF THE SINGLY-ENLARGED CUBE

The floor paid `16` because its Poincaré input reads `A` on `□̃̃`.  The drift reads `A` one block
layer forward only (`LocDrift.pathSite_mem_block_or_next` at `i = 1`), so it pays `4`.  Proof shape
REUSED verbatim from `LocFeed.bondsOn_tilde2_mult_le_sixteen`, with one `tilde` instead of two. -/

theorem bondsOn_tilde_mult_le_four {ι : Type*} [DecidableEq ι] (hell : 0 < ell)
    (hdvd : ∀ μ : Fin 3, ell ∣ (L μ + 1)) (𝒞 : Finset ι) (Y : ι → Finset (CSite L ell))
    (hdisj : ∀ i ∈ 𝒞, ∀ j ∈ 𝒞, i ≠ j → Disjoint (Y i) (Y j)) (b : Bond L) :
    (𝒞.filter (fun i => b ∈ bondsOn (tilde hdvd (Y i)))).card ≤ 4 := by
  obtain ⟨z0, hz0⟩ := exists_owner hell hdvd b.1
  have hcongr : 𝒞.filter (fun i => b ∈ bondsOn (tilde hdvd (Y i)))
      = 𝒞.filter (fun i => z0 ∈ tilde hdvd (Y i)) := by
    refine Finset.filter_congr (fun i _ => ?_)
    exact ⟨fun h => (mem_bondsOn_iff_owner _ b hz0).mp h,
      fun h => (mem_bondsOn_iff_owner _ b hz0).mpr h⟩
  rw [hcongr]
  exact tilde_mult_le_four hdvd 𝒞 Y hdisj z0

/-! ## §5 — THE SUMMATION: the drift priced from PER-CUBE GAUGED data alone -/

/-- **THE PER-CUBE DRIFT PRICE.**

Pairwise-disjoint cubes, ONE UNRELATED GAUGE PER CUBE, and a smallness bound holding only cube by
cube for the LOCALLY GAUGED background.  The conclusion is at the ORIGINAL `U` and the ORIGINAL `A`:
no global gauge is formed, no global smallness is used, and the sum on the left counts each
plaquette exactly once when the family covers (`plaqsOn_family_card_eq_one`).

>  `∑_i ∑_{p ∈ □_i} ‖(D_U − D_{1^{γ_i⁻¹}})A(p)‖² ≤ 128·α²·∑_b ‖A b‖²`

`128 = 32·4`, both factors named in §3 and §4.  **The reference is the cube's own pure gauge, not
the flat background** — that is the whole content of the statement, and `DriftNoGo` proves the
difference cannot be removed. -/
theorem global_drift_from_percube_gauges {ι : Type*} [DecidableEq ι]
    (hell2 : 2 ≤ ell) (hdvd : ∀ μ : Fin 3, ell ∣ (L μ + 1))
    (U : PeriodicLinkConfiguration (Matrix.specialUnitaryGroup (Fin 2) ℂ) L)
    (A : Bond L → SuTwo) (α : ℝ) (hα0 : 0 ≤ α)
    (𝒞 : Finset ι) (Y : ι → Finset (CSite L ell)) (γ : ι → GaugeFn L)
    (hdisj : ∀ i ∈ 𝒞, ∀ j ∈ 𝒞, i ≠ j → Disjoint (Y i) (Y j))
    (hclass : ∀ i ∈ 𝒞, ∀ b ∈ bondsOn (Y i), RMapLipschitz.frobNorm
      (((periodicGaugeTransform (γ i) U) b : Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℂ) - 1) ≤ α) :
    ∑ i ∈ 𝒞, ∑ p ∈ plaqsOn (Y i), ‖relDrift U (pureGauge (gaugeInv (γ i))) A p‖ ^ 2
      ≤ 128 * α ^ 2 * bondEnergy A := by
  have hell : 0 < ell := by omega
  have hstep : ∑ i ∈ 𝒞, ∑ p ∈ plaqsOn (Y i), ‖relDrift U (pureGauge (gaugeInv (γ i))) A p‖ ^ 2
      ≤ ∑ i ∈ 𝒞, 32 * α ^ 2 * ∑ b ∈ bondsOn (tilde hdvd (Y i)), ‖A b‖ ^ 2 :=
    Finset.sum_le_sum (fun i hi =>
      local_relDrift_le hell2 hdvd U A (γ i) α hα0 (Y i) (hclass i hi))
  have hmul := sum_family_le 𝒞 (fun i => bondsOn (tilde hdvd (Y i))) (fun b => ‖A b‖ ^ 2)
    (fun _ => sq_nonneg _) 4 (bondsOn_tilde_mult_le_four hell hdvd 𝒞 Y hdisj)
  have hbe : bondEnergy A = ∑ b : Bond L, ‖A b‖ ^ 2 := rfl
  have hfac : ∑ i ∈ 𝒞, 32 * α ^ 2 * ∑ b ∈ bondsOn (tilde hdvd (Y i)), ‖A b‖ ^ 2
      = 32 * α ^ 2 * ∑ i ∈ 𝒞, ∑ b ∈ bondsOn (tilde hdvd (Y i)), ‖A b‖ ^ 2 := by
    rw [Finset.mul_sum]
  have hc : (0 : ℝ) ≤ 32 * α ^ 2 := by positivity
  have hchain : 32 * α ^ 2 * ∑ i ∈ 𝒞, ∑ b ∈ bondsOn (tilde hdvd (Y i)), ‖A b‖ ^ 2
      ≤ 32 * α ^ 2 * ((4 : ℕ) * ∑ b : Bond L, ‖A b‖ ^ 2) :=
    mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left hmul hc
  rw [hfac] at hstep
  refine hstep.trans (hchain.trans (le_of_eq ?_))
  rw [hbe]
  push_cast
  ring

/-! ## §6 — CONTROLS: the left-hand side counts each plaquette EXACTLY once -/

/-- Pairwise-disjoint cubes meet each plaquette at most once (its OWNING block lies in at most one
cube).  Shape reused from `LocFeed.coarseOn_mult_le_one`. -/
theorem plaqsOn_mult_le_one {ι : Type*} [DecidableEq ι] (hell : 0 < ell)
    (hdvd : ∀ μ : Fin 3, ell ∣ (L μ + 1)) (𝒞 : Finset ι) (Y : ι → Finset (CSite L ell))
    (hdisj : ∀ i ∈ 𝒞, ∀ j ∈ 𝒞, i ≠ j → Disjoint (Y i) (Y j))
    (p : PeriodicLatticePlaquette L) :
    (𝒞.filter (fun i => p ∈ plaqsOn (Y i))).card ≤ 1 := by
  obtain ⟨z0, hz0⟩ := exists_owner hell hdvd p.1
  refine Finset.card_le_one.mpr (fun i hi j hj => ?_)
  by_contra hne
  have hi' := Finset.mem_filter.mp hi
  have hj' := Finset.mem_filter.mp hj
  exact (Finset.disjoint_left.mp (hdisj i hi'.1 j hj'.1 hne)
    ((mem_plaqsOn_iff_owner (Y i) p hz0).mp hi'.2)) ((mem_plaqsOn_iff_owner (Y j) p hz0).mp hj'.2)

/-- A covering family meets each plaquette at least once. -/
theorem plaqsOn_cover {ι : Type*} [DecidableEq ι] (hell : 0 < ell)
    (hdvd : ∀ μ : Fin 3, ell ∣ (L μ + 1)) (𝒞 : Finset ι) (Y : ι → Finset (CSite L ell))
    (hcov : ∀ z : CSite L ell, ∃ i ∈ 𝒞, z ∈ Y i) (p : PeriodicLatticePlaquette L) :
    1 ≤ (𝒞.filter (fun i => p ∈ plaqsOn (Y i))).card := by
  obtain ⟨z0, hz0⟩ := exists_owner hell hdvd p.1
  obtain ⟨i, hi𝒞, hiY⟩ := hcov z0
  exact Finset.card_pos.mpr ⟨i, Finset.mem_filter.mpr ⟨hi𝒞, (mem_plaqsOn_iff_owner (Y i) p hz0).mpr hiY⟩⟩

/-- **NO DOUBLE COUNTING AND NO OMISSION.**  On a disjoint COVERING family the outer sum of
`global_drift_from_percube_gauges` visits every plaquette exactly once — so its left-hand side is
the honest global drift energy with the reference varying by cube, not an inflated or a partial
sum. -/
theorem plaqsOn_family_card_eq_one {ι : Type*} [DecidableEq ι] (hell : 0 < ell)
    (hdvd : ∀ μ : Fin 3, ell ∣ (L μ + 1)) (𝒞 : Finset ι) (Y : ι → Finset (CSite L ell))
    (hdisj : ∀ i ∈ 𝒞, ∀ j ∈ 𝒞, i ≠ j → Disjoint (Y i) (Y j))
    (hcov : ∀ z : CSite L ell, ∃ i ∈ 𝒞, z ∈ Y i) (p : PeriodicLatticePlaquette L) :
    (𝒞.filter (fun i => p ∈ plaqsOn (Y i))).card = 1 :=
  le_antisymm (plaqsOn_mult_le_one hell hdvd 𝒞 Y hdisj p) (plaqsOn_cover hell hdvd 𝒞 Y hcov p)

/-- **AND THEN THE FAMILY SUM IS THE GLOBAL SUM** — stated at a COMMON gauge, where the summand no
longer depends on `i` and the identification is exact.  This is the sense in which §5's left-hand
side is a global quantity. -/
theorem family_sum_eq_global {ι : Type*} [DecidableEq ι] (hell : 0 < ell)
    (hdvd : ∀ μ : Fin 3, ell ∣ (L μ + 1)) (𝒞 : Finset ι) (Y : ι → Finset (CSite L ell))
    (hdisj : ∀ i ∈ 𝒞, ∀ j ∈ 𝒞, i ≠ j → Disjoint (Y i) (Y j))
    (hcov : ∀ z : CSite L ell, ∃ i ∈ 𝒞, z ∈ Y i)
    (U : PeriodicLinkConfiguration (Matrix.specialUnitaryGroup (Fin 2) ℂ) L)
    (A : Bond L → SuTwo) (γ : GaugeFn L) :
    ∑ i ∈ 𝒞, ∑ p ∈ plaqsOn (Y i), ‖relDrift U (pureGauge (gaugeInv γ)) A p‖ ^ 2
      = ∑ p : PeriodicLatticePlaquette L, ‖relDrift U (pureGauge (gaugeInv γ)) A p‖ ^ 2 := by
  rw [sum_family_count 𝒞 (fun i => plaqsOn (Y i))
    (fun p => ‖relDrift U (pureGauge (gaugeInv γ)) A p‖ ^ 2)]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun p _ => ?_)
  rw [plaqsOn_family_card_eq_one hell hdvd 𝒞 Y hdisj hcov p]
  norm_num

/-- **THE PRICE IN OPERATOR FORM, AND ITS PROVENANCE.**  `√128 = 8√2 = 2·(4√2)`: the per-cube drift
price is exactly TWICE the global one, and the factor `2` is `√4`, the enlarged-cube bond
multiplicity of §4 — not an estimate.  Stated as compiled arithmetic so no number here rests on
prose. -/
theorem drift_price_factorisation :
    (8 * Real.sqrt 2) ^ 2 = 128 ∧ (128 : ℝ) = 32 * 4 ∧ 8 * Real.sqrt 2 = 2 * (4 * Real.sqrt 2) := by
  have h2 : Real.sqrt 2 * Real.sqrt 2 = 2 := Real.mul_self_sqrt (by norm_num)
  refine ⟨by nlinarith [h2], by norm_num, by ring⟩

/-- **THE SINGLETON FAMILY MEETS §5's HYPOTHESES** — one cube per coarse site is pairwise disjoint
and covers, so §5 is not conditioned on an unsatisfiable geometry.  (`LocFeed.singleton_family_ok`,
REUSED rather than restated, and re-exposed here so a reader of this module sees it.) -/
theorem singleton_family_ok_here :
    (∀ i ∈ (Finset.univ : Finset (CSite L ell)), ∀ j ∈ (Finset.univ : Finset (CSite L ell)),
      i ≠ j → Disjoint ({i} : Finset (CSite L ell)) ({j} : Finset (CSite L ell)))
    ∧ (∀ z : CSite L ell, ∃ i ∈ (Finset.univ : Finset (CSite L ell)),
        z ∈ ({i} : Finset (CSite L ell))) :=
  singleton_family_ok

